## Alarming Recall Data
With 543 recalls this year alone, the food industry is facing scrutiny over safety practices. A troubling 173 of these are Class I recalls, indicating a reasonable probability of serious health consequences. This brings the all-time recall counter to 901, painting a stark picture of persistent issues in food safety protocols.

## Recent Highlights
### Salmonella in Seasonings
JCB Flavors, LLC, has been linked to multiple recalls due to Salmonella contamination in their seasoning products. This follows a pattern of negligence resulting in Class I recalls.

### Metal in Ice Cream
Straus Family Creamery's ice cream products were found to be potentially contaminated with metal pieces, categorizing this under a Class II recall.

### Allergen Mislabeling
Market of Choice Inc's vegan kale caesar salad failed to list sesame in their ingredients, a significant lapse for those with allergies. This misstep led to a Class II recall.

## Brand Performance
Recurring offenders highlight systemic issues in quality control. Moonlight Packing Corporation and Ghirardelli Chocolate Company both rank poorly with 11 and 10 recalls respectively, predominantly Class I, earning them a failing grade in food safety.

## Monthly Recap
May saw a peak in recalls with 173 incidents, whereas June numbers have thankfully decreased to 43 so far. However, with the pace at which new issues arise, this could easily change.

Stay informed and prioritize safety: keep an eye on recalls and check your pantry for affected items.
